course: dictionary
lesson: 5619
title: Many meanings of like
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Like is a small word with many jobs, so the words around it tell you which job it does. «A setback means a failure, made to sound like a small step back.» Here like means similar to: the failure is made to sound similar to a small step back.
explain: «Bubbles start at tiny places like scratches or specks.» Like means for example: scratches and specks are examples of tiny places. Check by swapping in for example, or similar to, and see which one still makes sense.
explain: «Carbon dioxide traps heat like a blanket.» A blanket keeps you warm by holding heat in, so like means in the same way as a blanket. When you meet like, ask: is it being compared, or is it giving examples?
fact: Like can be a verb: to like something is to enjoy it or think it is good.
fact: «Would like» is a polite way to say you want something: «I would like a glass of water, please.»
fact: Like can mean for example, or similar to: «fruit like apples and pears» and «sings like a bird».
fact: A like can also be a noun: it is a click that shows you enjoy a post online.
fact: In casual talk, like can mean about before a number, as in «like 20 people came», which means about 20, not exactly 20.
exercise: «Carbon dioxide traps heat like a blanket.» What does like mean here? | Enjoys | *Similar to, in the way a blanket does | Exactly the same as a sheet | Would want
exercise: Jayden says, «like 20 people came». What does like mean? | *About, so roughly 20 | Twenty people who liked it | Twenty people who were late | Exactly 20
exercise: «Bubbles start at tiny places like scratches or specks.» What does like mean? | Enjoys | *For example | Would want | Similar to a sheet of glass
test: «I would like a glass of water, please.» What does would like show? | *Wanting something politely | Enjoying water forever | Liking the glass | Making a noise
test: «Mia got forty likes on her post.» What is a like? | A safe place to hide | *A click that shows you enjoy a post online | A type of cake | A prize for being polite
exam: In a survey, 12 of 30 children said they like apples. Determine the number of respondents expressing a preference for apples. | 42 | *12 | 18 | 30
